{"assets":[],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"1934","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"E. Weird LCM Operations"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"2 seconds"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"256 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Given an integer $$$n$$$, you construct an array $$$a$$$ of $$$n$$$ integers, where $$$a_i = i$$$ for all integers $$$i$$$ in the range $$$[1, n]$$$. An operation on this array is defined as follows:"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"ordered":false},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" Select three distinct indices $$$i$$$, $$$j$$$, and $$$k$$$ from the array, and let $$$x = a_i$$$, $$$y = a_j$$$, and $$$z = a_k$$$. "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" Update the array as follows: $$$a_i = \\operatorname{lcm}(y, z)$$$, $$$a_j = \\operatorname{lcm}(x, z)$$$, and $$$a_k = \\operatorname{lcm}(x, y)$$$, where $$$\\operatorname{lcm}$$$ represents the least common multiple. "}],"kind":"list_item"}],"kind":"list"},{"kind":"text","text":" Your task is to provide a possible sequence of operations, containing at most $$$\\lfloor \\frac{n}{6} \\rfloor + 5$$$ operations such that after executing these operations, if you create a set containing the greatest common divisors (GCDs) of all subsequences with a "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"size greater than $$$1$$$"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":", then all numbers from $$$1$$$ to $$$n$$$ should be present in this set."},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"After all the operations $$$a_i \\le 10^{18}$$$ should hold for all $$$1 \\le i \\le n$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"We can show that an answer always exists."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first line contains one integer $$$t$$$ ($$$1 \\le t \\le 10^2$$$) — the number of test cases. The description of the test cases follows."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first and only line of each test case contains an integer $$$n$$$ ($$$3 \\leq n \\leq 3 \\cdot 10^{4}$$$) — the length of the array."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"It is guaranteed that the sum of $$$n$$$ over all test cases does not exceed $$$3 \\cdot 10^{4}$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"output_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first line should contain an integer $$$k$$$ ($$$0 \\leq k \\leq \\lfloor \\frac{n}{6} \\rfloor + 5$$$) — where $$$k$$$ is the number of operations."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The next $$$k$$$ lines should contain the description of each operation i.e. $$$3$$$ integers $$$i$$$, $$$j$$$ and $$$k$$$, where $$$1 \\leq i, j, k \\leq n$$$ and all must be distinct."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"samples"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Example"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n3\n3\n4\n7\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n1\n1 2 3\n1\n1 3 4\n3\n3 5 7\n5 6 7\n2 3 4"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"note"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Note"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the third test case, $$$a = [1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7]$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"First operation"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"$$$i = 3$$$, $$$j = 5$$$, $$$k = 7$$$"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"$$$x = 3$$$, $$$y = 5$$$, $$$z = 7$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"$$$a = [1, 2, \\operatorname{lcm}(y,z), 4, \\operatorname{lcm}(x,z), 6, \\operatorname{lcm}(x,y)]$$$ = $$$[1, 2, \\color{red}{35}, 4, \\color{red}{21}, 6, \\color{red}{15}]$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Second operation"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"$$$i = 5$$$, $$$j = 6$$$, $$$k = 7$$$"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"$$$x = 21$$$, $$$y = 6$$$, $$$z = 15$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"$$$a = [1, 2, 35, 4, \\operatorname{lcm}(y,z), \\operatorname{lcm}(x,z), \\operatorname{lcm}(x,y)]$$$ = $$$[1, 2, 35, 4, \\color{red}{30}, \\color{red}{105}, \\color{red}{42}]$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Third operation"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"$$$i = 2$$$, $$$j = 3$$$, $$$k = 4$$$"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"$$$x = 2$$$, $$$y = 35$$$, $$$z = 4$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"$$$a = [1, \\operatorname{lcm}(y,z), \\operatorname{lcm}(x,z), \\operatorname{lcm}(x,y), 30, 105, 42]$$$ = $$$[1, \\color{red}{140}, \\color{red}{4}, \\color{red}{70}, 30, 105, 42]$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Subsequences whose GCD equal to $$$i$$$ is as follows"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"$$$\\gcd(a_1, a_2) = \\gcd(1, 140) = 1$$$"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"$$$\\gcd(a_3, a_4) = \\gcd(4, 70) = 2$$$"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"$$$\\gcd(a_5, a_6, a_7) = \\gcd(30, 105, 42) = 3$$$"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"$$$\\gcd(a_2, a_3) = \\gcd(140, 4) = 4$$$"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"$$$\\gcd(a_2, a_4, a_5, a_6) = \\gcd(140, 70, 30, 105) = 5$$$"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"$$$\\gcd(a_5, a_7) = \\gcd(30, 42) = 6$$$"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"$$$\\gcd(a_2, a_4, a_6, a_7) = \\gcd(140, 70, 105, 42) = 7$$$"}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"document"},"index":"E","problemCode":"1934E","schema":2,"sourceKind":"html","sourceUrl":"https://codeforces.com/contest/1934/problem/E"}